<title>DENMARK: SAS strike threat looms after talks falter.</title>
<headline>SAS strike threat looms after talks falter.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of the union representing ground staff at Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) were meeting on Wednesday morning to decide whether to strike after wage talks broke down overnight.</p>
<p>&quot;We are disappointed at the short-sightedness shown by SAS management in negotiations. SAS has thrown away its only chance to establish constructive collaboration,&quot; the LFF aviation staff union said in a statement.</p>
<p>The union is threatening strike action from March 7.</p>
</text>
